DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260617T143000
SUMMARY:AT at Hot Springs to the Rich Mountain Fire Tower\; 12.5 mile Fitn
 ess Loop Hike.
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**MEETUP OPTIONS:**\n8:15 AM To ca
 rpool at Weaverville walmart parking\, lower level parking on the right. *
 *OTHERWISE\,** meet at the trailhead parking area @ 8:55 AM. Right turn ju
 st before the bridge at Hot Springs\; quick left under the bridge to the r
 iverside parking on the right. Please comment if you plan to carpool.\n\n*
 *DISTANCE:** 12.5- 13 miles.\n**ELEVATION GAIN**: Approximately 3\,200'.\n
 '\nThis loop hike begins at the riverside parking area at Silvermine Rd. W
 e will take the AT south to the Rich Mountain Fire Tower (see attached pic
 ) spur and return on the Round Top Trail. The out bound hike {approximatel
 y 8 miles} has 2 extended climbs. The first is up and beyond Lover's Leep 
 near Hot Springs\, and the second begins at Tanyard Gap to the Fire Tower 
 spur trail (total elevation gain of approximately 3\,200'. The return we w
 ill take the Round Top Trail to loop back which is a gradual (knee friendl
 y) descent to a left on the French Broad the river road for about 1/2 mile
  back to the parking area.\n\n**Hike** **Highlights** include beautiful hi
 gh ridge-line views overlooking the French Broad River Valley (picture)\, 
 rocky outcrops at Lovers Leap\, an old waterfilled tobacco field reservoir
 \, and long range moutain views from the fire tower.\n\n**PACE**: We hike 
 at a steady pace averaging 2.5 MPH on longer climbs with brief regrouping 
 as needed and at trail intersections\, and 3- 3+mph pace on level and down
 hill sections. This is for conditioned hikers. Please know your hiking abi
 lities and be capable of hiking this distance\, elevation\, and pace\, BEF
 ORE SIGNING ON.\n\n**DOGS:** Well-behaved dogs are welcome. There is water
  available at the reservoir and small active step-over springs. The final 
 phase is along the relatively flat shoulder of the French Broad River).\n\
 n**RSVP CANCELATION:** IF YOU SIGN UP FOR THIS HIKE\, OR THE WAITLIST\, an
 d CHANGE YOUR PLANS\, CANCEL YOUR RSVP TO FREE UP YOUR RESERVED SPOT FOR O
 THER HIKERS. THE WAITLIST REMAINS ACTIVE UNTIL 8 AM HIKE DAY SO YOU MAY BE
  MOVED ON UNTIL THAT TIME.\n\n**WEATHER**: Cancellation due to weather wil
 l be made on or before 7:15 am on the day of the hike.\n\n**\\*HIKE LEVELS
 :**\nLevel 1: 0-600'\; Level 2: 600-900'\; Level 3: 900-1200'\; Level 4: 1
 200-1500'\; Level 5: 1500-1800'\; \\*LEVEL 6 1800-2100'\; \\*LEVEL 7\; 210
 0-2400'\;\nLevel 8\; 2400-2700'\; Level 9\; 2700-3000'\; Level 10\; **3000
 -4000**'\;\nULTIMATE HIKES > 4000'\n\n**Release of Liability:**\nThe organ
 izer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The functio
 n of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or partic
 ipate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree 
 to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, a
 s a result of\, and associated with this event. In addition\, you acknowle
 dge that you agree to the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.com/terms
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315226641
 /
