DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260617T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260617T163000
SUMMARY:Flat Laurel Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis is one of the most popular cr
 eek hikes near Asheville. Note this is not the Flat Laurel Creek Trail\, i
 t is a creek hike. It begins at NC Hwy. 215 near the confluence of Flat La
 urel Creek and the West Fork of the Pigeon River (35.3283\, -82.9093). We 
 will ascend past numerous rapids and a few impressive waterfalls. We will 
 be in the creek or rock hopping most of the day. The requirements are a go
 od sense of balance\, comfortable shoes with good traction\, and ability o
 r interest to hike and climb in a creek. Good swimming holes abound\, and 
 a few waterslides. The pace will be relaxed and we will take a short break
  one of the many scenic spots for lunch. After finishing the ascent we wil
 l trail hike up to the Black Balsam parking lot\, where cars will be left 
 for this shuttle. You will have the option to hike up Big Sam Mountain (ov
 er 6K) for the view. However\, the group will proceed directly to the park
 ing by Black Balsam.\n\nWe will climb 800 feet and hike approx. 3 miles.\n
 We will be meeting at the Black Balsam parking lot at 9:30 am.\n\nAny ques
 tions I can be reached or text at 828 231-3581.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315249876
 /
