DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260617T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260617T210000
SUMMARY:Wednesday night Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Pow
 hatan Rec Area\nWeather: No rain in forecast\, I'll let you know if it's r
 aining\, and/or cancelled.\nI did this hike series for many years before 2
 022\, but I did it as a high-speed hike\, and I am now doing it as a moder
 ate speed hike. This is a numbers limited event and I expect people who si
 gn-up to show up. Late cancellations\, and those that don't show up are bu
 mping other interested hikers\, and they will not be allowed on future hik
 es.\nIf all goes well\, I will try to post a hike most weeks\, and for day
 s Tue or Wed\, distance\, and start location\, like switching between Hard
  Times trail-head and Bent Creek River Park\, may change.\nThe current rou
 te is about 5.5 miles.\nPlease folks\, this is intended as a moderate pace
 d hike\, and we'd like all attendees to keep up with the hike leader(s). T
 his hike is intended as a workout hike for people to get in condition to d
 o weekend hikes.\nModerate paced means 22-24 min miles\, or 2 ½ mph.\nAs 
 such\, we do not take breaks\, take in views\, or snap photos along the wa
 y. Please make sure you're able to keep up with the group. This hike has a
 lways served as a good chance to get exercise during the week\, meet new p
 eople\, and create interest for weekend enjoyment hikes. It's a great intr
 oduction to the AHG family.\nNo need to RSVP "No" or "not attending" unles
 s changing from a "Yes."\nPlease read the full description before RSVPing\
 , and only sign up if you are sure you can go. Thanks in advance for keepi
 ng your RSVP up-to-date and not being a last-minute cancellation or no-sho
 w. This is an ongoing issue with Meetups and often keeps people on waitlis
 ts from being able to attend our hikes.\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Po
 whatan Rec Area\nFollow signs off of Brevard Rd (Rt 191) to Lake Powhatan 
 Rec Area. The road is Bent Creek Ranch Rd. to Wesley Branch Rd. Follow sig
 ns to Lake Powhatan until you come to Hard Times Trailhead on your left\, 
 2.5 miles. It is very clearly marked. Parking is very limited at the trail
 head but there’s a paved pull-off just before the Hard Times trailhead a
 nd more parking just beyond at the Ledford Branch trailhead. We will acces
 s Bent Creek forest by way of Hard Times Trail and do some combination of 
 loop and out and back.\nArrive at the trailhead BY 6:00. Because it is a w
 eeknight hike\, we are unable to wait for latecomers\, fighting daylight.\
 n\\*\\*\\*If you are running behind\, please post a comment on this Meetup
  page by 5:45 pm. There is no cell service at the parking lot\, so if we d
 on't have any advance notice of you running late by 5:45\, we can't get an
 y notifications at the trailhead and we will not wait for you.\nWe start t
 he hike at 6:00\, rarely do we get much later than that.\n• Wear closed-
 toed footwear appropriate for hiking. The trail will consist of dirt\, roc
 ks\, roots\, mud and mulch.\n• Bring plenty of water.\n• Bring rain ge
 ar if a chance of rain is in the forecast.\nHeadlamps suggested\n• Dogs 
 on leashes the whole time are welcome. This is an active mountain bike are
 a and it can get messy with dogs running loose among hikers and mountain b
 ikers.\nPlease make sure to keep your RSVP up-to-date. You don't want to b
 e "that person" who cancels last minute or no-shows and keeps someone from
  joining in if there's a waitlist. Thanks for your consideration - it is a
 ppreciated!\nFeel free to post questions not covered in this description i
 n the comments section.\nThanks - we'll see you on the trail!\nDisclaimer 
 and Release of Liability:\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets t
 hat may have traffic and/or natural trails with roots\, rocks\, and steep 
 sections. Participants are responsible for their safety on streets and tra
 ils. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guid
 e. The function of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sig
 n up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and volu
 ntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages ar
 ising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. In addition\
 , you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.
 com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315242514
 /
