DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260619T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260619T120000
SUMMARY:Catawba Falls River and Ridge Loop - 3.6 Mi\, 850 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**RSVP opens Sunday\, Jun 14th\, 8
 :00 pm**\n\nA shorter hike for this week but I always enjoy Catawba Falls 
 and the challenge of 580 stair steps (equivalent to 30 stories). Some of t
 he stairs and platforms are open metal grate so some people and dogs may n
 ot like that but the views are spectacular. We will get a little earlier s
 tart as the parking lot and trail can be busy. We will complete our loop b
 y doing the Ridgeline Trail back to the bottom.\n\nhttps://www.alltrails.c
 om/trail/us/north-carolina/catawba-falls-river-loop\n\nHillmans in Old For
 t does open at 11am for lunch and I am planning to go there after the hike
 .\n\n***Dog Policy:*** Dogs are welcome but must be leashed and okay with 
 open metal grate stairs and platforms.\n\n***Guest Policy:*** If you'd lik
 e to bring a guest\, they should join the Asheville Hiking Group and sign 
 up for the hike on their own. Alternatively\, contact me in advance and as
 k if it's okay to bring a "+1" after you've made it onto the "Going" list.
  Depending on timing and demand\, I MAY be able to add your guest.\n\n**ME
 ET-UP TIME AND PLACE**\nPlease either meet at the Catawba Falls parking lo
 t at 9:00 or arrange to carpool with someone in your part of town. I can't
  figure out a good carpool location for this one\, post in the comments if
  you would like to carpool and what side of town you are located.\n\n**COU
 RTESY TO WAIT-LISTERS (Please abide!)**\nOnly sign up if you \\*TRULY\\* p
 lan to come. If you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going"
  as soon as possible so wait-listers will have sufficient notice. And plea
 se please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\nIf you're on the waiting list\, keep
  checking the evening before. Despite what I wrote above\, we always get l
 ast-minute dropouts.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll monitor National Weather Service
  forecasts for the hike area and email cancellation messages by 7:30 AM if
  the forecast is for more than a 50% chance of precipitation.\n\n**QUESTIO
 NS?**\nIf you have any questions\, message me through MeetUp until 8:00 AM
  the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy on the trail\, but you can try 
 to text or call me up to the start of the hike: 508-965-2333.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315253225
 /
